Syntrichia is a large, cosmopolitan genus of mosses in the family Pottiaceae. The genus name is of Greek origin for "with" and "hair", referring to the "twisted peristome united by a basal membrane".{{r|fna}}

{{As of|2020}}, the World Flora Online accepts 114 species in the genus Syntrichia:{{r|wfo}}

